[{:db/id 17592186133845 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-25a0a850-41a7-52c6-b901-d7ad5795dcd0" "question-4a15eeec-0407-53e4-9770-0d33f30c6d02" "question-9f3bf9f8-8f58-5a26-b354-f87af2b2eaa9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133660 :question/problem "A coin is biased so that the probability of it landing on heads is $0.4.$ The coin is tossed $7$ times. What is the mean number of times the coin lands on heads?" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times the coin lands on heads. \n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=7$ tosses\n\n- the probability of landing on heads for each toss is $p=0.4$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X\\sim B(7,0.4).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean of the number of times the coin lands on heads is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =(7)(0.4) \\\\  & =2.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133846 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-afe30003-2595-50a2-8b60-8382c78a5f23" "question-ed91a13d-0a09-59c4-bf60-d5ad7aad9e5f" "question-35949c7a-955a-5bb4-ba6f-41e4641f0ce2" "question-5f3fbaf6-b15b-53c6-9279-fcc77fd83e0b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133661 :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of arrows that hit the bull's eye.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=12$ shots\n\n- the probability of hitting the bull's eye for each arrow is $p=50\\%=0.5$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X\\sim B(12,0.5).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\n So, the variance of the number of arrows hitting the bull's eye is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =(12)(0.5)(1-0.5) \\\\  & =(6)(0.5) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133847 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cd4098b0-44f3-5628-89ab-3a85dd72d97e" "question-e3dde14a-c77b-5290-8e8d-52f3133ef7aa"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133662 :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times we get an even number.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=8$ rolls of the die\n\n- the probability of getting an even number (i.e., a $2,$ or $4$) on any roll of the die is\n\n$$\np=\\dfrac{2}{5} .\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X\\sim B\\left(8,\\dfrac25\\right).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the standard deviation is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{SD}[X] = \\sqrt{\\textrm{Var}[X]}=\\sqrt{np(1-p)},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the standard deviation of the number of times we get an even number is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{np(1-p)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}\\cdot (1-\\frac{2}{5})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1.92} \\\\  & =1.386\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134523 :question/problem "A fair six-sided die is rolled $7$ times. What is the mean of the number of times that the outcome of a single roll is a $2$ or a $3?$" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times a $2$ or $3$ is rolled.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=7$ rolls\n\n- the probability of getting a $2$ or $3$ on any roll of the die is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{2}{6}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(7,\\frac{1}{3}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean number of times we get a $2$ or a $3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =7\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133176 :answer-field/correct 17592186133177 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-25a0a850-41a7-52c6-b901-d7ad5795dcd0" :question/id #uuid "25a0a850-41a7-52c6-b901-d7ad5795dcd0" :question/math-academy-id "q-130755" :question/problem "A fair coin is tossed $20$ times. What is the mean number of tails that occur?" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of tails that occur. \n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=20$ tosses\n\n- since the coin is fair, the probability of landing on tails for each toss is $p=\\frac{1}{2}$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(20,\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean number of tails that occur is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =(20)(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-683d39b0-2df2-5987-be72-7499346048ee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-683d39b0-2df2-5987-be72-7499346048ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "683d39b0-2df2-5987-be72-7499346048ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6856acca-0b10-524b-b6c0-3ba8ffe6d469" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6856acca-0b10-524b-b6c0-3ba8ffe6d469" "answer-d743d3d8-0ac8-570a-9105-9ddcd4674ff4" "answer-c11f043f-d0d7-5366-8f1e-26ca782b6852" "answer-162e61c6-2672-53bc-b506-42b887c80bb5" "answer-0e4bdfc2-c0e9-5af4-abe8-067d3285da99"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6856acca-0b10-524b-b6c0-3ba8ffe6d469" :answer/id #uuid "6856acca-0b10-524b-b6c0-3ba8ffe6d469" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d743d3d8-0ac8-570a-9105-9ddcd4674ff4" :answer/id #uuid "d743d3d8-0ac8-570a-9105-9ddcd4674ff4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c11f043f-d0d7-5366-8f1e-26ca782b6852" :answer/id #uuid "c11f043f-d0d7-5366-8f1e-26ca782b6852" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-162e61c6-2672-53bc-b506-42b887c80bb5" :answer/id #uuid "162e61c6-2672-53bc-b506-42b887c80bb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e4bdfc2-c0e9-5af4-abe8-067d3285da99" :answer/id #uuid "0e4bdfc2-c0e9-5af4-abe8-067d3285da99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4a15eeec-0407-53e4-9770-0d33f30c6d02" :question/id #uuid "4a15eeec-0407-53e4-9770-0d33f30c6d02" :question/math-academy-id "q-84745" :question/problem "A fair eight-sided die is rolled $6$ times. What is the mean number of times that the outcome of a single roll is either $2,5,$ or $7?$" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times a $2$ or $5$ or $7$ is rolled.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=6$ rolls\n\n- the probability of getting a $2,5,$ or $7$ on any roll of the die is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(6,\\frac{3}{8}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean number of times we get a $2$ or a $5$ or a $7$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{3}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f267f788-271e-50ed-b945-f7aa83b94fe5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f267f788-271e-50ed-b945-f7aa83b94fe5" :answer-field/id #uuid "f267f788-271e-50ed-b945-f7aa83b94fe5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a438da50-52c7-56e2-9c8d-f943b1b94b8d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-af0cc9f5-7af8-51a0-9383-5f1def95ba05" "answer-2fec556e-e148-5b1e-97a7-c14be487a96c" "answer-4124268c-a67c-5426-94fd-b3b803fb7198" "answer-a438da50-52c7-56e2-9c8d-f943b1b94b8d" "answer-7cd5208b-1965-5729-baf4-fee9daa9dd7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af0cc9f5-7af8-51a0-9383-5f1def95ba05" :answer/id #uuid "af0cc9f5-7af8-51a0-9383-5f1def95ba05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2fec556e-e148-5b1e-97a7-c14be487a96c" :answer/id #uuid "2fec556e-e148-5b1e-97a7-c14be487a96c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4124268c-a67c-5426-94fd-b3b803fb7198" :answer/id #uuid "4124268c-a67c-5426-94fd-b3b803fb7198" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a438da50-52c7-56e2-9c8d-f943b1b94b8d" :answer/id #uuid "a438da50-52c7-56e2-9c8d-f943b1b94b8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7cd5208b-1965-5729-baf4-fee9daa9dd7b" :answer/id #uuid "7cd5208b-1965-5729-baf4-fee9daa9dd7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134522 :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of games that the team wins in a given season. \n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=12$ games\n\n- the probability of winning each game is $p=60%=0.6$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(12,0.6).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean of the number of games won is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =(12)(0.6) \\\\  & =7.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133170 :answer-field/correct 17592186133175 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-9f3bf9f8-8f58-5a26-b354-f87af2b2eaa9" :question/id #uuid "9f3bf9f8-8f58-5a26-b354-f87af2b2eaa9" :question/math-academy-id "q-130752" :question/problem "A tennis player has a $60%$ chance of winning each match in a $5$-match tournament. What is the mean number of matches that the player wins?" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of matches that the player wins.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=5$ matches\n\n- the probability of winning each match is $p=60%=0.6$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(5,0.6).$ \n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean number of matches that the player wins is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =(5)(0.60) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f16f7ac3-5d3e-5fdc-9751-952a50dea70c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f16f7ac3-5d3e-5fdc-9751-952a50dea70c" :answer-field/id #uuid "f16f7ac3-5d3e-5fdc-9751-952a50dea70c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bd86f57c-83b3-5a48-8104-a8621c5314c9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dde0bec6-b353-548b-907e-68f5d5bd0cf1" "answer-33ea5317-6dc1-5052-854f-8321410625d5" "answer-bd86f57c-83b3-5a48-8104-a8621c5314c9" "answer-25cf9ed6-5d80-5316-a85f-81ae68ce439d" "answer-d1ab47f4-d3b2-5da5-8dc7-53a759699c2e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dde0bec6-b353-548b-907e-68f5d5bd0cf1" :answer/id #uuid "dde0bec6-b353-548b-907e-68f5d5bd0cf1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33ea5317-6dc1-5052-854f-8321410625d5" :answer/id #uuid "33ea5317-6dc1-5052-854f-8321410625d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd86f57c-83b3-5a48-8104-a8621c5314c9" :answer/id #uuid "bd86f57c-83b3-5a48-8104-a8621c5314c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25cf9ed6-5d80-5316-a85f-81ae68ce439d" :answer/id #uuid "25cf9ed6-5d80-5316-a85f-81ae68ce439d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1ab47f4-d3b2-5da5-8dc7-53a759699c2e" :answer/id #uuid "d1ab47f4-d3b2-5da5-8dc7-53a759699c2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-afe30003-2595-50a2-8b60-8382c78a5f23" :question/id #uuid "afe30003-2595-50a2-8b60-8382c78a5f23" :question/math-academy-id "q-89408" :question/problem "A student answers a multiple-choice test choosing each answer at random. If the test has $20$ questions, and each question has $4$ possible answers with only one correct answer, what is the variance of the number of correct answers?" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of correct answers.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=20$ questions\n\n- the probability of selecting the correct answer in each question is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(20,\\frac{1}{4}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the variance of the number of correct answers is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =20\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (1-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-52456990-d9af-5708-ac87-59cf743cda06"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-52456990-d9af-5708-ac87-59cf743cda06" :answer-field/id #uuid "52456990-d9af-5708-ac87-59cf743cda06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2ba091fe-7823-5e7d-9d7b-281b39b773d4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-06c51642-996d-5135-870c-db34a80b53f0" "answer-a9d52625-39ab-5725-8e70-b6d00bcc3df8" "answer-07cebf32-de57-5ac9-b739-e5dd0c9c0388" "answer-2ba091fe-7823-5e7d-9d7b-281b39b773d4" "answer-e3dfbebf-b841-570e-af01-fbb924f4028f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06c51642-996d-5135-870c-db34a80b53f0" :answer/id #uuid "06c51642-996d-5135-870c-db34a80b53f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9d52625-39ab-5725-8e70-b6d00bcc3df8" :answer/id #uuid "a9d52625-39ab-5725-8e70-b6d00bcc3df8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07cebf32-de57-5ac9-b739-e5dd0c9c0388" :answer/id #uuid "07cebf32-de57-5ac9-b739-e5dd0c9c0388" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ba091fe-7823-5e7d-9d7b-281b39b773d4" :answer/id #uuid "2ba091fe-7823-5e7d-9d7b-281b39b773d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3dfbebf-b841-570e-af01-fbb924f4028f" :answer/id #uuid "e3dfbebf-b841-570e-af01-fbb924f4028f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ed91a13d-0a09-59c4-bf60-d5ad7aad9e5f" :question/id #uuid "ed91a13d-0a09-59c4-bf60-d5ad7aad9e5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-84691" :question/problem "An archer practices shooting $16$ arrows at a target. The archer has a $25%$ chance of hitting the bull's eye. What is the variance in the number of arrows that hit the bull's eye?" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of arrows that hit the bull's eye.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=16$ shots\n\n- the probability of hitting the bull's eye for each arrow is $p=25%=0.25$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(16,0.25).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\n So, the variance of the number of arrows hitting the bull's eye is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =(16)(0.25)(1-0.25) \\\\  & =(4)(0.75) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6dd00208-7396-5c4f-b789-94854564cf74"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6dd00208-7396-5c4f-b789-94854564cf74" :answer-field/id #uuid "6dd00208-7396-5c4f-b789-94854564cf74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5c47db2b-5f15-55e5-9a8b-2c3d636f340a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7a869429-9bb2-5c02-8d64-f99c5767b4a1" "answer-dbd63a4b-3acc-57cf-a187-bd16d36c3981" "answer-5c47db2b-5f15-55e5-9a8b-2c3d636f340a" "answer-12e44cce-8bca-5ac8-80a0-02abd7b3acd2" "answer-4fa3b4a5-cc48-533b-bd88-30d43ccbc53c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a869429-9bb2-5c02-8d64-f99c5767b4a1" :answer/id #uuid "7a869429-9bb2-5c02-8d64-f99c5767b4a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dbd63a4b-3acc-57cf-a187-bd16d36c3981" :answer/id #uuid "dbd63a4b-3acc-57cf-a187-bd16d36c3981" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c47db2b-5f15-55e5-9a8b-2c3d636f340a" :answer/id #uuid "5c47db2b-5f15-55e5-9a8b-2c3d636f340a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12e44cce-8bca-5ac8-80a0-02abd7b3acd2" :answer/id #uuid "12e44cce-8bca-5ac8-80a0-02abd7b3acd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fa3b4a5-cc48-533b-bd88-30d43ccbc53c" :answer/id #uuid "4fa3b4a5-cc48-533b-bd88-30d43ccbc53c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-35949c7a-955a-5bb4-ba6f-41e4641f0ce2" :question/id #uuid "35949c7a-955a-5bb4-ba6f-41e4641f0ce2" :question/math-academy-id "q-130763" :question/problem "There are $15$ gift boxes in a lucky gift machine, $6$ of which have a toy inside. After being picked, the gift box will be replaced by another one of the same value. Six kids are waiting in line for their turn to use it. What is the variance of the number of kids who get a toy?" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of kids who get a toy from the $6$ kids.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=6$ kids that are waiting in line for their turn to use the machine\n\n- since there are $6$ toys out of a total of $15$ gift boxes, then the probability that a kid gets a toy is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{6}{15}=\\frac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(6,\\frac{2}{5}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the variance of the number of kids who get a toy is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}\\cdot (1-\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\frac{3}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2eb92a3f-b47d-5759-a6af-54bb075b7bbd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2eb92a3f-b47d-5759-a6af-54bb075b7bbd" :answer-field/id #uuid "2eb92a3f-b47d-5759-a6af-54bb075b7bbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9fc18f76-a69e-5f09-9bb8-5aa58c800ea3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3f592e8f-e602-59d7-9c67-f601dddbe2e4" "answer-34b2a832-8cee-5042-b5f3-310a15c0aa97" "answer-85974766-468e-56eb-ba05-3ae52a9770fa" "answer-9fc18f76-a69e-5f09-9bb8-5aa58c800ea3" "answer-0a1da0bd-fbca-576c-9d98-2c5457624d78"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f592e8f-e602-59d7-9c67-f601dddbe2e4" :answer/id #uuid "3f592e8f-e602-59d7-9c67-f601dddbe2e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34b2a832-8cee-5042-b5f3-310a15c0aa97" :answer/id #uuid "34b2a832-8cee-5042-b5f3-310a15c0aa97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{18}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85974766-468e-56eb-ba05-3ae52a9770fa" :answer/id #uuid "85974766-468e-56eb-ba05-3ae52a9770fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{26}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9fc18f76-a69e-5f09-9bb8-5aa58c800ea3" :answer/id #uuid "9fc18f76-a69e-5f09-9bb8-5aa58c800ea3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{36}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a1da0bd-fbca-576c-9d98-2c5457624d78" :answer/id #uuid "0a1da0bd-fbca-576c-9d98-2c5457624d78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{36}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134524 :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of games that the team wins in a given season. \n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=20$ games\n\n- the probability of winning each game is $p=30%=0.3$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(20,0.3).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the variance of the number of games won is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =(20)(0.3)(1-0.3) \\\\  & =(6)(0.7) \\\\  & =4.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133182 :answer-field/correct 17592186133187 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-5f3fbaf6-b15b-53c6-9279-fcc77fd83e0b" :question/id #uuid "5f3fbaf6-b15b-53c6-9279-fcc77fd83e0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130764" :question/problem "A  fair octahedral die with sides labeled with numbers $1$ through $8$ is rolled $25$ times. What is the variance of the number of times we get a number divisible by $3?$" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of times we get a number divisible by $3.$\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=25$ rolls\n\n- the probability of getting a number divisible by $3$ (i.e., a $3$ or a $6$) on any roll of the die is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{2}{8}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(25,\\frac{1}{4}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the variance of the number of times we get a number divisible by $3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =25\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (1-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =25\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{75}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e996cded-d3ba-5d9b-afa2-4b9d6ae9a669"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e996cded-d3ba-5d9b-afa2-4b9d6ae9a669" :answer-field/id #uuid "e996cded-d3ba-5d9b-afa2-4b9d6ae9a669" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-887d0da7-9a5f-5923-9b6d-66308de467fe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-22e19085-b196-5d51-9863-47908156eca8" "answer-7a68e62a-0aac-5912-9c1d-b67fbcb42582" "answer-84bd8c58-0d9c-5855-a5e9-f875f7625f8c" "answer-887d0da7-9a5f-5923-9b6d-66308de467fe" "answer-5d31d5ff-3374-591a-a832-e6af48967464"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22e19085-b196-5d51-9863-47908156eca8" :answer/id #uuid "22e19085-b196-5d51-9863-47908156eca8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{125}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a68e62a-0aac-5912-9c1d-b67fbcb42582" :answer/id #uuid "7a68e62a-0aac-5912-9c1d-b67fbcb42582" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84bd8c58-0d9c-5855-a5e9-f875f7625f8c" :answer/id #uuid "84bd8c58-0d9c-5855-a5e9-f875f7625f8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{72}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-887d0da7-9a5f-5923-9b6d-66308de467fe" :answer/id #uuid "887d0da7-9a5f-5923-9b6d-66308de467fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{75}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d31d5ff-3374-591a-a832-e6af48967464" :answer/id #uuid "5d31d5ff-3374-591a-a832-e6af48967464" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{75}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cd4098b0-44f3-5628-89ab-3a85dd72d97e" :question/id #uuid "cd4098b0-44f3-5628-89ab-3a85dd72d97e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130883" :question/problem "An infectious flu virus is spreading through a school. The probability of a randomly selected student having the flu next week is $0.2.$ If a class has $23$ students, what is the standard deviation of the number of students having the flu next week? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of students having the flu next week.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=23$ students in the class\n\n- the probability of selecting a student having the flu next week is $0.2$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(23,0.2).$ \n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the standard deviation is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\sqrt{np(1-p)},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the standard deviation of the number of students having the flu next week is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{np(1-p)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(23)(0.2)(1-0.2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(23)(0.2)(0.8)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3.68} \\\\  & ≈1.918\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-33864cf7-e227-514a-994b-4fc9fe7a2ef7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-33864cf7-e227-514a-994b-4fc9fe7a2ef7" :answer-field/id #uuid "33864cf7-e227-514a-994b-4fc9fe7a2ef7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-396fb0b5-0937-562e-b292-d871531d1399" :answer-field/choices ["answer-396fb0b5-0937-562e-b292-d871531d1399" "answer-6519a704-3057-55cd-bed2-1c31319df05d" "answer-ce1c6f72-1a3a-554f-a780-a0e87d75a879" "answer-88059b2a-96be-58d2-99c2-cf71c816f2f4" "answer-155de04a-19c5-548a-9a38-8b17697942c4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-396fb0b5-0937-562e-b292-d871531d1399" :answer/id #uuid "396fb0b5-0937-562e-b292-d871531d1399" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.918" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6519a704-3057-55cd-bed2-1c31319df05d" :answer/id #uuid "6519a704-3057-55cd-bed2-1c31319df05d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.268" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce1c6f72-1a3a-554f-a780-a0e87d75a879" :answer/id #uuid "ce1c6f72-1a3a-554f-a780-a0e87d75a879" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.459" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88059b2a-96be-58d2-99c2-cf71c816f2f4" :answer/id #uuid "88059b2a-96be-58d2-99c2-cf71c816f2f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.897" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-155de04a-19c5-548a-9a38-8b17697942c4" :answer/id #uuid "155de04a-19c5-548a-9a38-8b17697942c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.250" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e3dde14a-c77b-5290-8e8d-52f3133ef7aa" :question/id #uuid "e3dde14a-c77b-5290-8e8d-52f3133ef7aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-130766" :question/problem "A new drug has a $64%$ probability of curing a patient within a week. If $50$ patients are treated, what is the standard deviation of the number of cured patients within a week? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of cured patients within a week.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=50$ patients in the sample\n\n- the probability that the new drug has cured a patient within a week is $p=64%=0.64$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(50,0.64).$ \n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the standard deviation is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\sqrt{np(1-p)},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the standard deviation of the number of cured patients within a week is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{np(1-p)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(50)(0.64)(1-0.64)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(50)(0.64)(0.36)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11.52} \\\\  & ≈3.394\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dbcc53b2-5f84-54cb-ad5c-a16cf94b1669"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dbcc53b2-5f84-54cb-ad5c-a16cf94b1669" :answer-field/id #uuid "dbcc53b2-5f84-54cb-ad5c-a16cf94b1669" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1bb983d5-2b7b-5838-bc2a-1666de24661f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-56c30780-7d07-5a2e-8519-69c2c3b635fa" "answer-e2f09300-30a4-50ed-beaa-6f1198f91050" "answer-1bb983d5-2b7b-5838-bc2a-1666de24661f" "answer-c8f2f5eb-23ba-5d31-9a39-bfc963eeafaa" "answer-8b38c6aa-a639-5c59-a6f3-477d51479873"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56c30780-7d07-5a2e-8519-69c2c3b635fa" :answer/id #uuid "56c30780-7d07-5a2e-8519-69c2c3b635fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.154" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2f09300-30a4-50ed-beaa-6f1198f91050" :answer/id #uuid "e2f09300-30a4-50ed-beaa-6f1198f91050" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.362" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1bb983d5-2b7b-5838-bc2a-1666de24661f" :answer/id #uuid "1bb983d5-2b7b-5838-bc2a-1666de24661f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.394" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8f2f5eb-23ba-5d31-9a39-bfc963eeafaa" :answer/id #uuid "c8f2f5eb-23ba-5d31-9a39-bfc963eeafaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.518" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b38c6aa-a639-5c59-a6f3-477d51479873" :answer/id #uuid "8b38c6aa-a639-5c59-a6f3-477d51479873" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.375" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135091 :tutorial/content "Remember that if $X$ is a binomial random variable in which there are $n$ experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment, then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\binom{n}{x} p^x (1-p)^{n-x}.\n$$\n\nIt can be shown that the expected value, variance, and standard deviation of a binomial random variable $X$ can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\ \\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\ \\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{np(1-p)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134018 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
